  "question": {
    "text": "The threshold frequency of metal is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. When the light of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is incident on the metal plate, the maximum velocity of photoelectron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. When the frequency of incident radiation is increased to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. the maximum velocity of photoelectrons emitted is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is:",
    "image": null
  },
